$[Import* std]
A macro may list keywords before its clauses: in a pattern, a keyword matches only the same identifier, so
clauses can tell `{!range 1 to 5}` from `{!range 1 below 5}`.
$[Macro !range [to below]
    {{a to b} {range a {+ b 1}}}
    {{a below b} {range a b}}]
${!range 1 to 3}
expect: [1, 2, 3]
${!range 1 below 3}
expect: [1, 2]
A keyword is not a pattern variable, and a template may use the same word as an ordinary name.
$[# to 10]
$[Macro !upto [to] {{to n} {range 0 n}}]
${!upto to 2}
expect: [0, 1]
$to
expect: 10
